@startuml canary-automode-touchpoints
title allow_in_auto_mode: where the change lands, master vs branch
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor #F4F4F4
  BorderColor #888888
}
skinparam ArrowColor #555555

left to right direction

package "master (532de02)" {
  rectangle "hook.py\nmain()\npermission_mode = hook_data.get(...)" as M1
  rectangle "hook.py\n_handle_command_tool /\n_handle_file_path_tool" as M2
  rectangle "resolve.py\nresolve_bash_permission_detailed /\nresolve_file_path_permission_detailed" as M3
  rectangle "resolve.py\n_resolve_one closure\n(ALSO the ask-floor stub probe --\nno separate seam to exclude it)" as M4 #FFE0E0
  rectangle "config.py\nConfiguration.resolve_permission_detailed\n(a METHOD -- test doubles must\nreimplement it)" as M5 #FFE8CC
  rectangle "config.py\n_resolve_permission_detailed_unclamped\n<b>override decided here</b>\nreason rewritten; matched_rule\nstill embedded IN reason text" as M6 #FFE8CC
  rectangle "hook.py\n_log_auto_mode_override_note\n(new WARNING-stream entry)" as M7

  M1 --> M2
  M2 --> M3
  M3 --> M4
  M4 --> M5
  M5 --> M6
  M6 --> M7
}

package "branch (a3e3f27)" {
  rectangle "hook.py\nmain()\npermission_mode = hook_data.get(...)" as B1
  rectangle "hook.py\n_handle_command_tool /\n_handle_file_path_tool" as B2
  rectangle "resolve.py\nresolve_bash_permission_detailed /\nresolve_file_path_permission_detailed" as B3
  rectangle "resolve.py\n_decide(cmd, mode) -- explicit param\n_resolve_one passes REAL mode\n_resolve_outer ALWAYS passes None" as B4 #E0FFE0
  rectangle "permission_resolution.py\nresolve_permission_detailed\n(a FREE FUNCTION -- test doubles\nunaffected, only 4-method duck type)" as B5 #E0FFE0
  rectangle "permission_resolution.py\n_resolve_unclamped\n<b>override decided here</b>\nreason rewritten; matched_rule stays\nCLEAN in its own RuntimeVerdict field" as B6 #E0FFE0
  rectangle "hook.py\n_log_auto_mode_override_note\n(new WARNING-stream entry)" as B7
  rectangle "test_architecture.py LAYERS +\n.pyscn.toml layer map\n(caught the new automode.py\nimport immediately)" as B8 #E0E0FF

  B1 --> B2
  B2 --> B3
  B3 --> B4
  B4 --> B5
  B5 --> B6
  B6 --> B7
  B5 ..> B8 : enforced by
}

note bottom of M4
  Master: no separate stub-probe
  seam. Closing the ask-floor
  hazard (deny rule matching an
  unverified inline-code stub,
  flagged allow_in_auto_mode)
  would need NEW plumbing through
  compound.py's resolve_one
  contract (~18 dependent test
  closures) -- documented as a
  known limitation, not fixed.
end note

note bottom of B4
  Branch: TOO-45 R1e had ALREADY
  split resolve_one / resolve_outer
  for an unrelated reason (audit-
  trail correctness). That seam
  let the SAME hazard be closed
  with one explicit parameter and
  a regression test -- demonstrated
  by execution (temporarily
  reverting the fix flips the test
  from pass to fail).
end note

@enduml
